# Advanced ORM

## Framework semantics

Complex filtering often needs subqueries/`exists`, association filtering via `matching`, and denormalized counters via CounterCache behavior. Prefer Query expressions over string SQL.

## Required behavior

- Encapsulate advanced query shapes in finders on the owning Table.
- Prefer `matching` / `notMatching` / subquery expressions over ad-hoc joins in controllers.
- Use CounterCache (or equivalent Behavior) for maintained counts — not controller increments.
- Keep raw SQL exceptional and bound; never concatenate user input.

## Anti-patterns

- Controller-built subquery graphs copied everywhere
- Manual counter updates scattered across actions when CounterCache fits
- Unbound string SQL

## Review checklist

- [ ] Advanced queries live in finders
- [ ] Counters have a single ownership strategy
- [ ] No SQL injection vectors
